      "message": "It might be preferable to do this split on the bluetooth audio AIDL provider side; for example like this (you wouldn\u0027t need AidlToAidlMiddleware, MTKBluetoothAudioProvider or the 500 lines above this in that file if qcom uses the AOSP AIDL interface): https://review.lineageos.org/c/LineageOS/android_hardware_mediatek/+/505223/4/aidl/bluetooth_audio/aidl_adapter/MTKBluetoothAudioProviderFactory.cpp#525 - simply branch if a given provider type is hardware or software and dispatch it to the different providers. Then software sessions get written to libbluetooth_audio_session.so\u0027s static memory, and hardware sessions get written to libbluetooth_audio_session_qti.so\u0027s static memory, so there\u0027s no need to change audio_bluetooth_hw or anything.",
